 In Search of Answers: Indian Women’s Voices from Manushi (London: Zed Books, , reprinted New Delhi: Horizon India Books, ); Radha Kumar,

 The History of Doing: An Illustrated Account of Movements for Women’s Rights and Feminism in India,  (New Delhi: Kali for Women, ); Julia Leslie (ed.),

 Roles and Rituals for Hindu Women (London: Pinter Press, ); Sara S. Mitter,

 Dharma’s Daughters (New Brunswick NJ: Rutgers University Press, ); Susie Tharu and K. Lalita (eds),

 Women Writing in India,  BC to the Early Twentieth Century (London: Pandora Press, ).

 On

 dalits : Barbara R. Joshi (ed.),

 Untouchable: Voices of the Dalit Liberation Movement (London: Zed Books, ); Mark Juergensmeyer,

 Religion as Social Vision: The Movement Against Untouchability (Berkeley: University of California Press, ); Dilip Hiro,

 The Untouchables of India,

 Report no.  (Minority Rights Group, ). See also 'Ram Chander’s Story’ in Tully,

 No Full Stops in India.

